A1. Night club owners do this without being arrested. ~ ROB
A4. An accelerator of the gay 90's. ~ WHIP
A8. It all started in an apple orchard. ~ LOVE
A12. A good dust collector. ~ EAR
A13. A good place to end it all. ~ RENO
A14. This kind of promise should have been written. ~ ORAL
A15. A pant. ~ DRAWER
A17. Bootleggers make an awful farce of this. ~ LAW
A19. The "Poor Indian's" first name. ~ LO
A20. If you win at poker, then you've done this. ~ WON
A21. The whole kit and caboodle. ~ ALL
A22. Hard to find with your hands in the air. ~ COP
A23. What most school teachers do with a ruler. ~ RULE
A25. This fellow kept under cover until the war was over. ~ SPY
A26. Some day this may be seven cents on the Interborough. ~ FARE
A27. A Mexican motor car. ~ ASS
A28. A salutation. ~ SIR
A29. What the run in the stocking did. ~ RAN
A30. Mama, after she's sawed in half. ~ MA
A31. A roll in the stocking. ~ DEPOSIT
A33. The first word of a coming citizen. ~ DA
A35. About the only thing a cat can throw. ~ FIT
A36. Wim and wigor. ~ PEP
A37. Where some young chickens get hard boiled. ~ POT
A38. Put this in the pay telephone to get even with central. ~ SLUG
A40. This usually goes with a pow. ~ WOW
A41. A glass in this form is worth looking into. ~ PANE
A42. The lone eagle. ~ TEN
A43. A political discussion. ~ GAS
A44. People this way are never against you. ~ FOR
A45. The morning after. ~ AM
A46. Part of a small eye. ~ DOT
A47. What the stuff right off the boat really is. ~ POISON
A50. The girl went out for a ride, and this is what she actually did. ~ RODE
A52. A prince from a great distance. ~ EMIR
A54. Spanish gold. ~ ORO
A55. Made in Hollywood, but it is not the real stuff. ~ SNOW
A56. This guy supported the donkey in Missouri. ~ REED
A57. The uplift of many poor fish. ~ NET

D1. Makes the bull more bullish. ~ RED
D2. Row boat fuel. ~ OAR
D3. Triplets broadcasting. ~ BRAWLS
D4. A bird. ~ WREN
D5. A pronoun. ~ HER
D6. When the maid says you're out, you're usually like this. ~ IN
D7. A repeater. ~ POLLY
D8. Spits, the day after. ~ LOW
D9. Conjunction. ~ OR
D10. Medals are awarded for this. ~ VALOR
D11. Do this and go to Elkton, Md. ~ ELOPE
